BetaScan
========

Asynchronous TCP port scanner with service detection and lightweight
fingerprinting.

Overview
--------
BetaScan supports IP addresses and domain names, resolves DNS automatically,
and reports port state (open/closed/filtered) plus service and version details
when available.

Author
------
Mohamed Riadh (Beta)

Features
--------
- Asynchronous TCP scanning with configurable concurrency
- Port presets (top 20/50/100) or custom ranges
- Service hints from well-known ports and banners
- Optional TLS probing with version/cipher and certificate metadata
- Table, JSON, or CSV output

Requirements
------------
- Python 3.9+ (3.10+ recommended)
- Standard library only (no external dependencies)

Setup
-----
1) Install Python from https://www.python.org/downloads/
2) Verify the interpreter:
   - Windows: python --version
   - Linux/macOS: python3 --version
3) Run from the project directory:

   python betascan.py <target> [options]

Usage
-----
python betascan.py <target> [options]

Examples
--------
Basic scan (default ports 1-1024):

  python betascan.py example.com

Custom port range:

  python betascan.py example.com --ports 1-1024,8080

Top ports preset (20/50/100):

  python betascan.py example.com --top 100

Show only open ports:

  python betascan.py example.com --top 100 --open-only

JSON output to file:

  python betascan.py example.com --top 100 --format json --output scan.json

CSV output to file:

  python betascan.py example.com --top 50 --format csv --output scan.csv

Options
-------
Option | Description | Default
--- | --- | ---
--ports <list> | Port list or ranges (e.g., 1-1024,8080) | 1-1024
--top <N> | Use curated common ports list (20, 50, 100) | -
--timeout <seconds> | Connection timeout | 1.5
--read-timeout <seconds> | Read timeout for banners and probes | 1.0
--workers <count> | Concurrent workers | 200
--retries <count> | Retry attempts for timeouts | 2
--backoff <seconds> | Delay between retries | 0.2
--rate <per-sec> | Limit new connections per second (0 = unlimited) | 0
--open-only | Show only open ports | false
--fingerprint / --no-fingerprint | Enable or disable fingerprinting | enabled
--tls / --no-tls | Enable or disable TLS probing | enabled
--format <table|json|csv> | Output format | table
--output <path> | Write output to file instead of stdout | -

Output Formats
--------------
- table: human-readable ASCII table
- json: structured report per target
- csv: flat rows suitable for spreadsheets

Exit Codes
----------
- 0: success
- 2: invalid arguments or target resolution error
- 130: interrupted by user (Ctrl+C)

Notes
-----
- Higher timeouts and retries improve accuracy at the cost of scan time.
- TLS probing includes protocol version, cipher, and certificate details when
  available.
- Use only on systems you own or have explicit permission to test.
